	 ('Sculpture – From Antiquity to the Middle Ages','from the Eighth Century BC to the Fifteenth Century',375,1999,544,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'3-8228-7059-5','this book was originally published in two volumes: PART I – The Great Art of Antiquity – from the Eighth Century BC to the Fifth Century AD, by Philippe Bruneau, Mario Torelli, Xavier Barral i Altet, edited by Jean-Luc Daval, ©1991 Editions d''Art Albert Skira S.A., Geneva (pages 1 – 240); PART II – The Great Art of the Middle Ages – from the Fifth Century to the Fifteenth Century, by Georges Duby, Xavier Barral i Altet, Sophie Guillot de Suduiraut, edited by Georges Duby and Jean-Luc Daval, ©1989 Editions d''Art Albert Skira S.A., Geneva (pages 241 – 544); © for this edition 1999 Benedict Taschen Verlag, GmbH, Köln, edited by Georges Duby and Jean-Luc Daval; translated from the French by Anthea Roll, Simon Knight and Andrew Wilson for First Editions Translations Ltd., Cambridge, UK (pages 1 – 240) and by Michael Heron (pages 241 – 544); printed in Austria; (prva od dve knjige; druga knjiga u kompletu: &quot;Sculpture – From the Renaissance to the Present Day&quot;, ID 1501); poklon Tanji za Markovo rođenje, od Darka i Ane, 17.7.2000.',0,1,1,1,0,253,340,45,1,NULL,0,0,0,1500,1,26),
	 ('Sculpture – From the Renaissance to the Present Day','from the Fifteenth Century to the Twentieth Century',375,1999,608,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'3-8228-7034-X','this book was originally published in two volumes: PART I – The Great Tradition of Sculpture – from the Fifteenth Century to the Eighteenth Century, by Bernard Ceysson, Geneviève Bresc-Bautier, Maurizio Fagiolo dell''Arco, François Souchal, ©1987 Editions d''Art Albert Skira S.A., Geneva (pages 1 – 298); PART II – The Adventure of Modern Sculpture – in the Nineteenth and Twentieth Centuries, by Antoinette Le Normand-Romain, Anne Pingeot, Reinhold Hohl, Jean-Luc Daval, Barbara Rose, Friedrich Meschede, ©1986 Editions d''Art Albert Skira S.A., Geneva (pages 298 – 608); © 1996 VG Bild-Kunst, Bonn, for the illustrations; © for this edition 1999 Benedict Taschen Verlag, GmbH, Köln; translation from the French: Michael Heron, Michael Taylor, translation from the Italian: James Emmons, translation from the German: André Marling, Michael Heron, Antony Wood for First Editions Translations Ltd., Cambridge, UK; printed in Austria; (druga od dve knjige; druga knjiga u kompletu: &quot;Sculpture – From Antiquity to the Middle Ages&quot;, ID 1500); poklon Tanji za magistraturu od Darka, 20.6.2000.',0,1,1,1,0,253,340,50,1,NULL,0,0,0,1501,1,26),
